.TH NYX-RUN 8 "2025" "NYX Framework" "NYX Manual"
.SH NAME
nyx-run \- execute NYX workflow files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nyx-run
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " workflow.json"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nyx-run
loads, validates, and executes a NYX workflow definition.
It parses a JSON workflow file into a directed acyclic graph (DAG)
of tool invocations, validates the graph, and executes steps in
topological order. Each step invokes a NYX tool in-process via the
global tool registry and wires results through the expression engine.
.PP
In human mode,
.B nyx-run
streams tool output live and prefixes it with step context so
operators can follow progress without waiting for the workflow to finish.
In JSON mode, a single structured result envelope is emitted to stdout.
.PP
Supports
.B for_each
fan-out (run a step once per array element) and
.B when
conditionals (skip steps based on previous results).
.PP
When a tool reports an error, the workflow records the step as
.B error
and exposes the tool's structured error details in the final output.
Downstream steps may still be skipped or executed depending on their
.B when
conditions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -J, --json
Emit a single JSON envelope to stdout. No banners, progress spinners,
or human-readable logs are written to stdout in this mode.
.TP
.BI -S " ID" "\fR,\fP --session " ID
Write workflow output to the given session ID under
.IR ~/.nyx/sessions/ .
.TP
.BI -V " KEY=VALUE" "\fR,\fP --var " KEY=VALUE
Override a workflow variable. Can be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BI -b " DIR" "\fR,\fP --bin-dir " DIR
Use an explicit NYX binary directory instead of resolving sibling tools
from the current executable path.
.TP
.B -d, --debug
Enable verbose workflow logging.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show version information.
.SH WORKFLOW FORMAT
Workflow files are JSON with three sections:
.TP
.B workflow
Metadata: id, name, version, description.
.TP
.B vars
Key-value parameters, overridable with \fB\-\-var\fR.
.TP
.B steps
Array of step objects, each with: id, tool, params, optional
for_each, optional when, optional meta.
.PP
Dependencies between steps are derived automatically from
\fB${step_id.field}\fR expressions in params, for_each, and when.
.SH EXPRESSION LANGUAGE
Expressions use \fB${...}\fR syntax:
.PP
.nf
${vars.subnet}
${sweep.results.hosts | filter alive == true}
${sweep.results.alive_count > 0}
${each.ip}
.fi
.PP
Pipe operations: filter, select, count, first, flat.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a workflow with live output:
.PP
.RS
.B nyx-run workflows/net-discovery.json
.RE
.PP
Run in JSON mode:
.PP
.RS
.B nyx-run -J workflows/net-discovery.json
.RE
.PP
Override a variable:
.PP
.RS
.B nyx-run workflows/net-discovery.json --var subnet=10.0.0.0/24
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.nyx/sessions/
Session storage for workflow and tool envelopes.
